
DONE (2026-07-16 rework):
    - [x] Volumetric 3D custom garment — the flat "puffed paper" mesa is now a rounded,
      torso-centred dome (per-row half-ellipse cross-section + distance-field edge taper +
      baked ambient-occlusion vertex colours + a woven-cloth normal grain), Z-only so inches
      stay exact. Catalog tee/hoodie bodies now use a MeshPhysicalMaterial cloth sheen.
      Verify: node scripts/inflate-verify.mjs (asserts real dome curvature, not just a bulge).
    - [x] Cross-device AR — replaced the old camera-overlay/overlay-mannequin AR entirely.
      Now: bake the design onto a male/female mannequin -> export GLB + USDZ (three exporters)
      -> upload to Cloudflare R2 via a Worker -> a SHORT scannable QR (/v/{id}) -> a lean viewer
      page (own three GLTFLoader preview) with a "View in your space" button that launches
      NATIVE AR (Android Scene Viewer / iOS Quick Look). Cross-device + works for photo/custom
      designs. Verify: scripts/ar-verify.mjs (GLB/USDZ export) + scripts/ar-worker-verify.mjs
      (Worker + R2 round-trip). Deploy needs `wrangler r2 bucket create tshop-ar` + a 30-day
      lifecycle rule (see README).
    - [x] Mobile — Canva two-tier select: a slim selection bar (edit / duplicate / delete)
      that never covers the artwork, expanding to the full properties sheet only on "Edit";
      the sheet hides while dragging. De-collided the zoom HUD vs the front/back/sleeve switch.
    - [x] Sleeve print side — Side = front | back | sleeve; a shared flat-sleeve illustration
      (4x4in print area); sleeve flows through 2D editing, 300-DPI print, zones, the order
      count and the side switcher (catalog only — custom garments stay front/back). The 3D
      preview shows front/back only.
    - [x] Area-aware pricing — optional per-garment areaTiers (<=A4 is the standard, +$0; <=A3
      +$4; oversize +$9) wired to the real placed-artwork area; the flat default stays
      byte-identical. Delete `areaTiers` from a rule to make that garment flat again.

